    "note": "Three named defects, all inside the pre-registered event set. (a) A record in `cash_mergers` whose (symbol, effective_date) also appears in `stock_and_cash_mergers` carries only the CASH leg of a mixed-consideration deal; dividing that cash leg by the pre-close price manufactures a catastrophic loss the actual shareholder never took, because they also received stock. (b) Warrant, unit and rights tickers are admitted by a bare ^[A-Z]{1,5}$ shape test and are cashed out at a cent. (c) Section 4's exclusion 3 forbids bars AFTER the effective date but says nothing about a name that stopped trading long BEFORE it, so a halted or sanctioned ADR can enter with a multi-year holding period. Each is a definitional error in this pre-registration, not a finding about merger arbitrage; each is reported rather than repaired, because repairing it after the verdict is exactly the move a freeze exists to forbid."
  },
